Journey: Home quote premium matches the rating rules, the API and the database
Id: quote-home-premium
Tags: @portal @rating @regression @integration
Role: policyholder
Risk: 5
Requirements: RATE-1, RATE-2, RATE-4
Variables: sumInsured=450000, region=COAST, propertyAge=42, ncdYears=3

Log in
Click the "Get a quote" link
  Expect the page contains "Get a quote"
Select "Home insurance" from the Product dropdown
Fill the "Sum insured (GBP)" field with ${sumInsured}
Select "Coast" from the Region dropdown
Fill the "Property age (years)" field with ${propertyAge}
Fill the "No-claims years" field with ${ncdYears}
Click the "Calculate premium" button
  Expect the page contains "Premium breakdown"
Read the premium breakdown into premium
Capture the text of testid=quote-ref as quoteRef

# 1. the screen against the underwriting manual (a reusable sub-journey with parameters and returns)
Run journey "expected-premium" with product="HOME", sumInsured=${sumInsured}, region=${region}, riskAge=${propertyAge}, noClaimsYears=${ncdYears} and store the result as expected
Expect ${premium.basePremium} == ${expected.base}
Expect ${premium.loadingPct} == 12
Expect ${premium.discount} == ${expected.discount}
Expect ${premium.tax} == ${expected.tax}
Expect ${premium.totalPremium} == ${expected.total}

# 2. the same risk rated through the broker API
Call API "POST ${API_URL}/v1/quotes" as broker with body '{"product":"HOME","sumInsured":${sumInsured},"region":"${region}","riskAge":${propertyAge},"noClaimsYears":${ncdYears}}' and store as apiQuote
Expect the apiQuote response status is 201
Expect response apiQuote "$.premium.totalPremium" equals "${expected.total}"
Expect response apiQuote "$.premium.netPremium" equals "${expected.net}"

# 3. the quote the portal saved, in the database
Get the first row of query "SELECT * FROM quotes WHERE id = '${quoteRef}'" on claims as saved
Expect ${saved.channel} equals "PORTAL"
Expect ${saved.total_premium} == ${expected.total}
Expect ${saved.tax} == ${expected.tax}
